@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/fa-toast/api"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Toast: API" ComponentName="FaToastHost + FaToastService" DocSlug="fa-toast" />

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/fa-toast" ShowWiring="true" />

<h2>FaToastHost</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>Position</code></td><td><code>FaToastPosition</code></td><td>default <code>TopRight</code> — <code>TopLeft</code> · <code>TopCenter</code> · <code>TopRight</code> · <code>BottomLeft</code> · <code>BottomCenter</code> · <code>BottomRight</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>No <code>CssClass</code>/<code>AdditionalAttributes</code> on this component — mount it once, typically in your root layout.</p>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">FaToastService</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Signature</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>Show</code></td><td><code>void Show(string text, FaAlertVariant variant = FaAlertVariant.Info, int durationMs = 4000)</code></td><td>the one method — inject this service anywhere and call it to fire a toast</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>No output to read back — there's nothing to bind, it's fire-and-forget. See <a href="/fa-toast/wiring">Wiring up</a> for the required DI registration.</p>
